questions.a:
Rule: all synchronous code first → then all microtasks (promise callbacks, code after await) → then macrotasks (setTimeout).
```js
console.log("A");
setTimeout(() => console.log("B"));
Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log("C"));
console.log("D");
// A D C B
```

concepts.body:
```js
console.log(1);
setTimeout(() => console.log(2), 0);
Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log(3));
(async () => { console.log(4); await null; console.log(5); })();
console.log(6);
// 1 4 6 3 5 2
```
Sync first (1, 4, 6). Then microtasks in order queued (3, then 5). Then the timeout (2).

