Discriminated union: `data` only exists in the success case, so TypeScript stops you reading it while loading.
```ts
type State<T> =
  | { status: "idle" }
  | { status: "loading" }
  | { status: "error"; error: string }
  | { status: "success"; data: T };
if (s.status === "success") s.data; // OK only here
```

