questions.a:
Attach one listener to a parent and use `event.target` (often `closest()`) to see which child was clicked, relying on events bubbling up.
```js
list.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
  const row = e.target.closest("li[data-id]");
  if (row) select(row.dataset.id);
});
```
Benefits: fewer listeners (memory), works for items added later, simpler cleanup.

