questions.a:
Plan out loud: data → state (selected category) → derived values (filtered list, total) → UI states.
```tsx
type Tx = { id: string; label: string; category: string; amountPence: number };

function Transactions({ txs }: { txs: Tx[] }) {
  const [cat, setCat] = useState("all");
  const categories = useMemo(() => ["all", ...new Set(txs.map((t) => t.category))], [txs]);
  const shown = cat === "all" ? txs : txs.filter((t) => t.category === cat);
  const total = shown.reduce((s, t) => s + t.amountPence, 0);
  const fmt = (p: number) => new Intl.NumberFormat("en-GB", { style: "currency", currency: "GBP" }).format(p / 100);

  return (
    <section>
      <label>Category{" "}
        <select value={cat} onChange={(e) => setCat(e.target.value)}>
          {categories.map((c) => <option key={c}>{c}</option>)}
        </select>
      </label>
      {shown.length === 0 ? <p>No transactions.</p> : (
        <ul>{shown.map((t) => <li key={t.id}>{t.label}: {fmt(t.amountPence)}</li>)}</ul>
      )}
      <p><b>Total: {fmt(total)}</b></p>
    </section>
  );
}
```
Mention: amounts in pence (integers), derived state instead of extra useState, empty state, accessibility (label), then tests.

```tsx
function Converter({ rate }: { rate: number }) {   // e.g. GBP → EUR
  const [gbp, setGbp] = useState("");
  const n = Number(gbp);
  const valid = gbp !== "" && Number.isFinite(n) && n >= 0;
  return (
    <div>
      <label>Amount (GBP)
        <input inputMode="decimal" value={gbp} onChange={(e) => setGbp(e.target.value)} />
      </label>
      {gbp && !valid && <p role="alert">Enter a valid amount</p>}
      <output>{valid ? (n * rate).toFixed(2) + " EUR" : "–"}</output>
    </div>
  );
}
```
Talk about: validation, decimal input on mobile, rounding (and doing money maths in minor units), fetching the rate (loading/error, staleness), a swap button, and tests for edge cases (empty, "abc", negative, huge numbers).
